    "created_at": "2018-08-01T23:53:19Z",
    "updated_at": "2018-08-01T23:53:19Z",
    "body": "The reason to make it parseable is that there are situations where a user's normal interface collides with the assigned accessKeyLabel. Assuming the browser is user-friendly enough not to over-ride the normal interface, software that helps the user reassign things so they are available but not clashing will want to parse the value.\r\n\r\n(For example, using VoiceOver on Mac, almost all accessKeyLabel values will clash with commands in voiceover and therefore be disabled. While it is feasible to write Safari-specific code that only worries about dealing with the clash in Safari/VoiceOver, it would be more useful to have a more general ability to detect the assigned keys and decide if they clash, and where required change the underlying accesskey).",
    "author_association": "NONE",
    "pin": null,
